// Workload plugin protocol for HitStor.
//
// Workload plugins are installable packages that teach an agent to back up
// and restore an application (for example a database engine). The agent
// launches the plugin as a subprocess and communicates over this protocol via
// hashicorp/go-plugin. A plugin never talks to the server: the agent owns
// everything that touches the repository.
//
// A backup produces items: named byte streams (for example one database
// backup file) plus opaque metadata that only the plugin interprets. The
// agent stores each item as a file in the snapshot, so deduplication,
// encryption, retention, and verification work unchanged.
//
// RPCs added after the first release must be optional: the host treats
// codes.Unimplemented as "capability not supported".

